# Kilo Code Rules — Motion Designer Pipeline

You are the engineering agent for an automated **vertical-video pipeline** built on
**Remotion 4 + Three.js (React Three Fiber) + Tailwind CSS (v4)**. This file is your
operating contract. It is authoritative for every task in this repository.

## 1. Mandatory rule reading (enforce strictly, in order)

Before writing or changing any code, read and obey the modular rules:

- `rules/01_motion_design.md` — frame-bound animation (`useCurrentFrame()`, `spring()`), 30 FPS, 1080x1920, easing physics.
- `rules/02_project_bundle_parsing.md` — parsing `input/<project>/{prompt.txt,styleguide.json,content.json,sources/}`.
- `rules/03_audio_and_sfx.md` — frame-accurate SFX triggers and audio ducking.
- `rules/04_threejs_standards.md` — R3F lighting, cameras, performance standards.
- `rules/05_ai_producer_workflow.md` — how a Producer turns raw briefs/assets into a valid bundle.

These rules win over ad-hoc templates and defaults. If a request conflicts with a
rule, follow the rule and flag the conflict — never silently ignore a rule.

## 2. Hard constraints (non-negotiable)

- **Canvas is 1080x1920 @ 30 FPS**, default duration **300 frames** (composition id `MainVideo`).
- **Deterministic animation only.** Every animated value derives from `useCurrentFrame()`
  (and `useVideoConfig()`). FORBIDDEN: `setTimeout`, `setInterval`, `requestAnimationFrame`,
  `Date.now()`, `performance.now()`, CSS transitions/keyframes, and unseeded `Math.random()`
  (use Remotion's `random()`).
- **No real-time audio APIs.** Never use `AudioContext` or Web Audio scheduling. Audio uses
  Remotion `<Audio>` + `<Sequence from={int}>` at 30 fps, with frame-driven gain envelopes.
- **`staticFile()` for every runtime asset.** Never pass OS/relative filesystem paths to
  Remotion media; assets are served from `public/` (bundles are generated into `public/bundles/`).
- **`input/` is read-only** to the engine. Only the AI Producer workflow (rule 05) creates new
  bundles there. Never mutate or delete existing bundles.
- **All renders go to `output/`.** Never write renders anywhere else.
- Never edit files in `rules/` unless a task explicitly asks you to.
- 3D confined to `src/components/3d/`; 2D UI in `src/components/ui/`; audio helpers in
  `src/components/audio/`; scenes in `src/scenes/`; scripts in `scripts/`.

## 3. Code quality guidelines

- **Strict TypeScript.** Zero `tsc` errors. No `any` (use `unknown` + guards). No unused
  imports, variables, or parameters (`noUnusedLocals` is on).
- **Frame-clamp every `interpolate()`**: pass `extrapolateLeft: "clamp"` and
  `extrapolateRight: "clamp"` unless an overshoot is intentional and documented.
- **Springs** always pass explicit `fps` and a `config`; guard `frame` to `>= 0`
  (`Math.max(0, frame - delay)`).
- **Three.js**: `frameloop="never"` with an explicit per-frame `gl.render()`; drive all
  motion from `useCurrentFrame()`; cap `dpr` to `[1, 2]`; no independent animation loops.
- **Mandatory error boundaries + Suspense for Three.js assets.** Any `<Canvas>` subtree that
  loads assets (`useGLTF`, `useTexture`, async) MUST be wrapped in a `<Suspense>` with a
  frame-stable fallback AND an error boundary that renders a deterministic fallback, so a
  slow or failed asset never breaks a frame or produces a blank/black render.
- No per-frame allocations (hoist `THREE.Vector3` etc.); reuse geometries/materials.
- Reuse existing components (`src/components/{ui,3d,audio}/`) instead of duplicating primitives.
- Never log secrets; never commit secrets or rendered media.

## 4. Verification gate (MANDATORY before reporting anything complete)

Before you consider any generated scene, component, rule, or script finished:

1. Run **`npm run lint`** (which executes `eslint src && tsc`).
   Equivalent: **`npx tsc --noEmit`** for types alone.
2. Fix **all** errors and warnings. Do not report completion with a failing lint/tsc.
3. When a visual change is made, also sanity-check with a still render:
   `npx remotion still MainVideo output/preview.png --frame=60`
   (or `npx remotion studio` for interactive review).

Report the lint/tsc result explicitly in your final message.

## 5. Project map

| Path | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| `input/<project>/` | Read-only bundles (`prompt.txt`, `styleguide.json`, `content.json`, `sources/`) |
| `input/_template/` | Reference bundle (kept in VCS; other bundles are git-ignored) |
| `output/` | Rendered MP4s + previews (contents git-ignored, folder kept) |
| `rules/` | Modular AI instruction markdown (01–05) |
| `src/Root.tsx` | Composition registry (`MainVideo`) |
| `src/scenes/` | Scene components |
| `src/components/ui` / `3d` / `audio` | 2D, 3D, audio building blocks |
| `src/utils/projectLoader.ts` | Bundle loader (registry-backed) |
| `src/utils/bundleRegistry.generated.ts` | AUTO-GENERATED; never edit by hand |
| `scripts/` | Automation (`generate-bundles.mjs`, `watcher.ts`, producer prompt) |
| `public/bundles/` | Generated from `input/` by `npm run bundles` (git-ignored) |

## 6. Commands

- Preview studio: `npx remotion studio` (or `npm run dev`, which runs `bundles` first)
- Lint / typecheck: `npm run lint` (`eslint src && tsc`)
- Register bundles + copy assets: `npm run bundles`
- Render: `npx remotion render src/index.ts MainVideo output/<name>.mp4 --props='{"projectId":"<id>"}'`
- Watch & auto-render new bundles: `npm run watch`
- Bundle only: `npm run build`

The Remotion **entry point is `src/index.ts`** (it calls `registerRoot`); `src/Root.tsx`
exports the root component and is NOT a valid CLI entry.

## 7. Pipeline behavior

- **Producer (rule 05)**: raw brief + assets → valid bundle in `input/<project_id>/`.
- **Registry**: `npm run bundles` scans `input/`, inlines bundle JSON into
  `bundleRegistry.generated.ts`, and copies `sources/` into `public/bundles/<id>/`.
- **Renderer**: `scripts/watcher.ts` watches `input/`, validates new/changed bundles, runs
  the registry step, then renders `output/<id>.mp4` with `--props={"projectId":"<id>"}`.
- A bundle is only renderable after it is registered; always run `npm run bundles` before render.

## 8. Environment notes

- `node_modules` is hosted on the `D:` drive via a directory junction; the npm cache is
  redirected to `D:` via `.npmrc`. Do **not** delete the junction or the cache config.
- `C:` has very little free space — avoid large artifacts outside `D:`.
